{"kind":"assert","text":"2026-09-07 simplification audit: orient Noseq around one confidential document app, and file five bounded backlog tasks.","body":{"all":"The user explicitly requested another codebase review for radical simplification, de-cluttering and clearer orientation, and asked that actionable findings be filed in the task list. This audit is read-only on source. Root read the current README, plan/status, package/CI configuration, compact and historical clients, live/archive/reconstruction outcome paths, recursive runners and the unmerged gate/assurance contract. Two bounded read-only architecture/product audits informed the review; root independently opened the cited code before filing tasks.\n\nInspected main: 1c158d8044cd53ceed5cd191f1f423613c3c571e. Inspected unmerged candidate: 9d36161fc086249d81a36e37a57ffff7d879f44e. A tracked .ts/.mjs/.html scan reports main src=3 files/35 lines, scripts=24/2287, tests=58/7273; candidate src=3/35, scripts=27/2681, tests=62/7559. Much real implementation lives under tests, so these numbers are code-location evidence, not a claim that those files are useless tests. The user-facing host is still an empty baseline. Existing full verification results are historical reports; no suites, builds or security experiments ran in this audit.\n\nFive actionable tasks follow: SIMPLIFY-01 decide the portable release-assurance boundary; SIMPLIFY-02 define the first confidential direct-document app milestone; SIMPLIFY-03 make the README/current runnable path clear; SIMPLIFY-04 replace current client inheritance and repeated post-authentication folding; SIMPLIFY-05 replace recursive runners with one explicit suite execution. Each task contains source evidence, scope, deletion or delivery goal, acceptance, effort/risk and dependencies. They are backlog entries, not instructions to start automatically or to change the frozen P1f candidate. Root must explicitly select a task before it is promised or implemented.\n\nRecommended order